{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "1da5489a-e8e3-4b6e-94e8-7e6818ce3fda",
        "name": "ReqRes API - QA Portfolio",
        "description": "## ReqRes API \u2013 QA Portfolio\n\nThis collection contains functional test cases for the [ReqRes](https://reqres.in) public API, organized as a QA portfolio to demonstrate API testing practices using Postman.\n\nThe tests cover the **Users** resource and are grouped into three modules:\n\n### Users - Search (GET)\n\nValidates the behavior of the `GET /api/users/{id}` endpoint across different scenarios:\n\n- **CT001.001** \u2013 Retrieve a user by a valid existing ID\n- **CT001.002** \u2013 Retrieve a user by a non-existent ID\n- **CT001.003** \u2013 Retrieve a user without authentication\n\n### Users - Creation (POST)\n\nValidates the behavior of the `POST /api/users` endpoint:\n\n- **CT002.001** \u2013 Create a user with valid data\n- **CT002.002** \u2013 Create a user without authentication\n- **CT002.003** \u2013 Create a user with an empty request body (Validation Finding)\n\n### Users - Update (PUT)\n\nValidates the behavior of the `PUT /api/users/{id}` endpoint:\n\n- **CT003.001** \u2013 Update an existing user with valid data\n- **CT003.002** \u2013 Update a user without authentication\n- **CT003.003** \u2013 Update a user with a non-existent ID (Validation Finding)\n- **CT003.004** \u2013 Update a user with an empty request body (Validation Finding)\n\n---\n\nEach test case follows a structured naming convention (`CT[module].[case]`) to make it easy to trace requirements and results. The collection uses environment variables (e.g., `{{baseUrl}}`, `{{api-key}}`) for environment management.",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
        "_exporter_id": "28586720"
    },
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "Users - Search (GET)",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "CT001.001 - Retrieve existing user by ID",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "x-api-key",
                                "value": "{{api-key}}",
                                "type": "text"
                            }
                        ],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/2",
                            "host": [
                                "{{baseUrl}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "users",
                                "2"
                            ]
                        }
                    },
                    "response": [],
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                                    "pm.test('Response must be valid JSON and have a body', function () { pm.response.to.be.withBody; pm.response.to.be.json; });",
                                    "pm.test('Response contains data object', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('data'); });",
                                    "pm.test('Returned user ID matches request (2)', function () { const jsonData = pm.response.json(); if (jsonData.data) { pm.expect(jsonData.data.id).to.eql(2); } });"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "name": "CT001.002 - Retrieve non-existent user by ID",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "x-api-key",
                                "value": "{{api-key}}",
                                "type": "text"
                            }
                        ],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/23",
                            "host": [
                                "{{baseUrl}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "users",
                                "23"
                            ]
                        }
                    },
                    "response": [],
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.test('Status code is 404', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(404); });",
                                    "pm.test('Response body is valid JSON', function () { pm.response.to.be.json; });",
                                    "pm.test('Response body is empty object', function () { const jsonData = pm.response.json(); pm.expect(Object.keys(jsonData).length).to.eql(0); });"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "name": "CT001.003 - Retrieve user without authentication",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/2",
                            "host": [
                                "{{baseUrl}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "users",
                                "2"
                            ]
                        }
                    },
                    "response": [],
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(401); });",
                                    "pm.test('Response indicates missing or invalid api key', function () { const res = pm.response.json(); pm.expect(res.error).to.be.oneOf(['missing_api_key', 'invalid_api_key']); });"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
